<title>USA: Calif. Gov. signs $71 mln fire protection bill.</title>
<headline>Calif. Gov. signs $71 mln fire protection bill.</headline>
<dateline>SACRAMENTO, Calif. 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>California Gov. Pete Wilson on Friday signed a $71 million measure to pay for fire protection services across the state.</p>
<p>The bill appropriates the funds for the California Department of Forestry and Fire Protection to pay for fire suppression costs incurred in the 1996-1997 fiscal year.</p>
<p>On Thursday, the state Assembly approved the measure.</p>
</text>
